I wrote:

>Lately I've had a lot of fun rediscovering NetHack 3.0 on my A3000,
>but the graphics characters representing open, closed, and locked
>doors look a little too much like walls under Dos 2.04.

>I tried just deleting the line "GRAPHICS=..." from NetHack.cnf, but
>that causes the game and the system to hang.  Does anyone have a
>favorite "GRAPHICS=" command which looks nice under 2.04?

Problem solved.  Quoting the latest installation instructions:

[stuff deleted]
	  "Copy the remainder of the files to NetHack:.  If you are using
	   the optional font, create a Hack subdirectory on NetHack:, and
	   copy "8" into it."

[Here's the important one:]
	7) AMIGA 3000 running AmigaDos 2.0 ONLY:
	   If you are using the optional font, you need to build a new
	   hack.font file:
		copy NetHack:hack FONTS: all
		FixFonts
		copy FONTS:hack.font NetHack:
		delete FONTS:hack all

Apparently 2.04 uses a different "*.font" file format.  Fixfonts
creates a new one from the "fonts:hack/8" file, placing the result in
"fonts:".  It is necessary to copy the result back to "Nethack:".

Before doing this, walls look like the letters AE (compressed into one
character), while closed doors are like A' and open doors are like A`.

